cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the functional locality harness, certificate schema, empirical laws, or public MoE reproduction scripts, please cite this release."
title: "Functional Locality in Sparse Mixture-of-Experts: Empirical Laws, Self-Falsified Predictors, Fail-Closed Certificates, and Open Multi-Architecture Reproduction"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kataguru/functional-locality-moe"
authors:
  - family-names: "Katajisto"
    given-names: "Jari"
    affiliation: "Kataguru Research"
keywords:
  - mixture-of-experts
  - sparse-moe
  - functional-locality
  - modular-fine-tuning
  - fail-closed-certificates
  - evaluation-metrology
  - non-determinism
abstract: >-
  An empirical investigation of routing locality (L1), functional locality (L2),
  and disjoint-support composition (L3) in Sparse Mixture-of-Experts models,
  including necessary-vs-sufficient failure analysis, candidate Law 7 cross-cartridge
  router dominance, self-falsified unweighted Law 2 vs. continuous early-layer exposure,
  machine-enforced JSON Schema Draft 2020-12 fail-closed certificates (7 mutation tests),
  and open reproduction on public Apache-2.0 MoE architectures.
